Guard against propagating past a locally UNSAT worker in OR-Tools CP-SAT 9.15.

Applies to tag v9.15 (551ad10d94835c99e5e1e684500d3db398c0e345). Generated
2026-09-13 for factorio-lab-to-blueprint. Built and verified the same day;
see docs/superpowers/evidence/2026-09-13-native-abort/ and README.md beside
this file. Not submitted upstream.

The abort: CHECK(!sat_solver_->ModelIsUnsat()) at the top of
LinearProgrammingConstraint::Propagate(). A shared-tree worker's level-zero
callbacks import bounds without propagating and return true; the shared-tree
sync callback then decodes a tree literal, the encoder adds level-zero
implication clauses, the pending propagation conflicts, the solver is marked
UNSAT, the encoder drops that status, and the callback still returns true.
The next propagation reaches the CHECK.

All three hunks test the pure getter ModelIsUnsat() and change nothing when
the worker is not UNSAT; every caller already handles a false return.

Apply with: git apply --check unsat-callback-guard.patch

diff --git a/ortools/sat/integer_search.cc b/ortools/sat/integer_search.cc
index 737a086..68938ac 100644
--- a/ortools/sat/integer_search.cc
+++ b/ortools/sat/integer_search.cc
@@ -1362,6 +1362,9 @@ IntegerSearchHelper::IntegerSearchHelper(Model* model)
       inprocessing_(model->GetOrCreate<Inprocessing>()) {}

 bool IntegerSearchHelper::BeforeTakingDecision() {
+  // A level-zero callback (or the code it triggers) may already have marked
+  // the local solver UNSAT while returning true; never propagate past that.
+  if (sat_solver_->ModelIsUnsat()) return false;
   DCHECK(sat_solver_->PropagationIsDone());

   // If we pushed root level deductions, we go back to level zero and call
@@ -1388,7 +1391,14 @@ bool IntegerSearchHelper::BeforeTakingDecision() {

   auto* level_zero_callbacks = model_->GetOrCreate<LevelZeroCallbackHelper>();
   for (const auto& cb : level_zero_callbacks->callbacks) {
-    if (!cb()) {
+    // Callbacks such as SharedTreeWorker::SyncWithSharedTree() can create
+    // integer literals whose level-zero implication clauses conflict with
+    // bounds imported by an earlier callback; SatSolver::AddProblemClause()
+    // then sets model_is_unsat_ but IntegerEncoder::AddImplications() drops
+    // that return value and the callback still returns true.  Propagating
+    // afterwards would reach LinearProgrammingConstraint::Propagate() and its
+    // CHECK(!sat_solver_->ModelIsUnsat()).
+    if (!cb() || sat_solver_->ModelIsUnsat()) {
       sat_solver_->NotifyThatModelIsUnsat();
       return false;
     }
diff --git a/ortools/sat/work_assignment.cc b/ortools/sat/work_assignment.cc
index 7cfdb79..ed71fea 100644
--- a/ortools/sat/work_assignment.cc
+++ b/ortools/sat/work_assignment.cc
@@ -1430,6 +1430,10 @@ bool SharedTreeWorker::SyncWithSharedTree() {
     assigned_tree_implications_.push_back(std::move(implications));
   }
   DCHECK(CheckLratInvariants());
+  // DecodeDecision() -> IntegerEncoder::GetOrCreateAssociatedLiteral() may add
+  // level-zero clauses whose propagation marks this worker UNSAT; the encoder
+  // discards that status, so report it here instead of returning true.
+  if (sat_solver_->ModelIsUnsat()) return false;
   return true;
 }

